{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And the blood shall be for you for a sign.</b> That you fulfill the commandment. Another interpretation: for a sign and a remembrance that they spilled your blood." "<b>And I will see the blood.</b> Even though it is inside — when HaShem commands His servants to do something or to speak something in His name, they speak as though HaShem Himself is speaking, for the agent of the sender is as the sender, and the end of the matter proves it: ולא יתן המשחית etc. But the bringing out was done by HaShem Himself, as our Sages said: ויוציאנו ה׳ — not by means of an angel. <b>[And I will see</b> — meaning, He will reckon it as though this seeing is in the heart.]" "<b>And I will pass over you.</b> And I stepped — as in ויפסחו על המזבח."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:11.449192371Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}